{"toolCallId":"call_352c520cafa547a5810e4a83a491e75e","status":"completed","content":[{"type":"content","content":{"type":"text","text":"--- callers ---\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/tests/test-phase-system.js:23:const RECOMMEND_SCRIPT = path.join(SKILL_ROOT, 'runtime', 'cli', 'spec', 'recommend-level.sh');\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/tests/snapshots/scaffold-golden-snapshots.vitest.ts.snap:577:<!-- FILL: Turn each gate into a check a command can answer. Keep the boxes unticked until they pass. GOOD: \\`rg -n 'quiet' recommend-level.sh\\` prints the new branch before the task starts. WEAK: The team agrees the plan is ready. -->\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/tests/snapshots/scaffold-golden-snapshots.vitest.ts.snap:594:<!-- FILL: Name the pattern in three words, then list the one component that changes. GOOD: Single script branch. The component is \\`recommend-level.sh\\`. WEAK: Standard architecture. -->\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/tests/snapshots/scaffold-golden-snapshots.vitest.ts.snap:736:<!-- FILL: Write one measurable outcome per line. A command can prove it. GOOD: \\`recommend-level.sh --quiet --loc 500 --files 15\\` prints one line and exits 0. WEAK: The feature is successful. -->\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/tests/snapshots/scaffold-golden-snapshots.vitest.ts.snap:804:<!-- FILL: Replace the sample tasks with the real setup steps. Each task names a file and a verify command. GOOD: T001 Read the output block in \\`recommend-level.sh\\`. Verify: \\`rg -n 'Recommended Level'\\` prints one line. WEAK: T001 Set up the project. -->\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/tests/snapshots/scaffold-golden-snapshots.vitest.ts.snap:1008:<!-- FILL: Turn each gate into a check a command can answer. Keep the boxes unticked until they pass. GOOD: \\`rg -n 'quiet' recommend-level.sh\\` prints the new branch before the task starts. WEAK: The team agrees the plan is ready. -->\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/tests/snapshots/scaffold-golden-snapshots.vitest.ts.snap:1025:<!-- FILL: Name the pattern in three words, then list the one component that changes. GOOD: Single script branch. The component is \\`recommend-level.sh\\`. WEAK: Standard architecture. -->\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/tests/snapshots/scaffold-golden-snapshots.vitest.ts.snap:1042:<!-- FILL: Name each surface the change touches. Write \\`not a consumer\\` when it does not read the change. Write \\`N/A\\` or delete the whole addendum when no fix surface applies. GOOD: \\`recommend-level.sh\\`: owns the output. Action: update. WEAK: Various files. -->\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/tests/snapshots/scaffold-golden-snapshots.vitest.ts.snap:1256:<!-- FILL: Write one measurable outcome per line. A command can prove it. GOOD: \\`recommend-level.sh --quiet --loc 500 --files 15\\` prints one line and exits 0. WEAK: The feature is successful. -->\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/tests/snapshots/scaffold-golden-snapshots.vitest.ts.snap:1381:<!-- FILL: Replace the sample tasks with the real setup steps. Each task names a file and a verify command. GOOD: T001 Read the output block in \\`recommend-level.sh\\`. Verify: \\`rg -n 'Recommended Level'\\` prints one line. WEAK: T001 Set up the project. -->\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/tests/snapshots/scaffold-golden-snapshots.vitest.ts.snap:1463:<!-- FILL: Write one check per file rule. A command must answer it. GOOD: CHK-010 [P0] \\`bash -n recommend-level.sh\\` exits 0. WEAK: Code is clean. -->\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/tests/snapshots/scaffold-golden-snapshots.vitest.ts.snap:1698:<!-- FILL: Turn each gate into a check a command can answer. Keep the boxes unticked until they pass. GOOD: \\`rg -n 'quiet' recommend-level.sh\\` prints the new branch before the task starts. WEAK: The team agrees the plan is ready. -->\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/tests/snapshots/scaffold-golden-snapshots.vitest.ts.snap:1715:<!-- FILL: Name the pattern in three words, then list the one component that changes. GOOD: Single script branch. The component is \\`recommend-level.sh\\`. WEAK: Standard architecture. -->\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/tests/snapshots/scaffold-golden-snapshots.vitest.ts.snap:1732:<!-- FILL: Name each surface the change touches. Write \\`not a consumer\\` when it does not read the change. Write \\`N/A\\` or delete the whole addendum when no fix surface applies. GOOD: \\`recommend-level.sh\\`: owns the output. Action: update. WEAK: Various files. -->\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/tests/snapshots/scaffold-golden-snapshots.vitest.ts.snap:2039:<!-- FILL: Write one measurable outcome per line. A command can prove it. GOOD: \\`recommend-level.sh --quiet --loc 500 --files 15\\` prints one line and exits 0. WEAK: The feature is successful. -->\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/tests/snapshots/scaffold-golden-snapshots.vitest.ts.snap:2191:<!-- FILL: Replace the sample tasks with the real setup steps. Each task names a file and a verify command. GOOD: T001 Read the output block in \\`recommend-level.sh\\`. Verify: \\`rg -n 'Recommended Level'\\` prints one line. WEAK: T001 Set up the project. -->\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/tests/snapshots/scaffold-golden-snapshots.vitest.ts.snap:2273:<!-- FILL: Write one check per file rule. A command must answer it. GOOD: CHK-010 [P0] \\`bash -n recommend-level.sh\\` exits 0. WEAK: Code is clean. -->\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/tests/snapshots/scaffold-golden-snapshots.vitest.ts.snap:2580:<!-- FILL: Turn each gate into a check a command can answer. Keep the boxes unticked until they pass. GOOD: \\`rg -n 'quiet' recommend-level.sh\\` prints the new branch before the task starts. WEAK: The team agrees the plan is ready. -->\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/tests/snapshots/scaffold-golden-snapshots.vitest.ts.