{"toolCallId":"call_a1e00a0a62164321a085e9503ec6464a","status":"completed","content":[{"type":"content","content":{"type":"text","text":".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/feature-catalog/tooling-and-scripts/spec-lifecycle-automation.md:6:  - recommend-level.sh\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/feature-catalog/tooling-and-scripts/spec-lifecycle-automation.md:19:The lifecycle is intentionally split into focused commands. `recommend-level.sh` scores a task and recommends the documentation level and optional phasing strategy. `create.sh` materializes the parent spec, optional child phases, or versioned subfolders. `upgrade-level.sh` raises an existing spec folder to a richer documentation level without discarding authored content. `calculate-completeness.sh` measures placeholder burn-down and optional content quality, `check-completion.sh` enforces checklist completion and evidence rules, and `archive.sh` archives or restores completed work with a completeness gate.\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/feature-catalog/tooling-and-scripts/spec-lifecycle-automation.md:29:Level recommendation is handled by `recommend-level.sh` as a standalone scoring tool. It accepts estimated LOC, file count, and risk flags for auth, API, database, and architectural work, converts those inputs into a 100-point score, maps the result to Level 0 through Level 3, and separately computes whether phased execution is recommended. Phase scoring uses its own 50-point signal model and only recommends phases when the phase score crosses the threshold and the recommended documentation level is Level 3 or higher.\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/feature-catalog/tooling-and-scripts/spec-lifecycle-automation.md:31:Spec creation is handled by `create.sh`, which defaults to Level 1 unless `--level` is provided. The script creates `scratch/`, copies the level template set, optionally creates a git branch and writes `description.json` when the Node helper is available. For root and phase scaffolds it then derives `graph-metadata.json` through the graph backfill, which warns and continues when the derivation fails. It also replaces the template placeholder trigger phrases of 18 document kinds with phrases built from the packet slug, and it runs full post-create validation only when `SPECKIT_POST_VALIDATE=1` is set. Beyond normal folder creation, it supports versioned subfolders with `--subfolder`, phased parent-plus-child creation with `--phase`, append-mode phase growth with `--parent`, named child phases with `--phase-names`, and Level 3 sharded spec sections with `--sharded`. The current implementation exposes complexity fields in its output, but the script itself still depends on explicit `--level` input rather than invoking `recommend-level.sh` automatically.\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/feature-catalog/tooling-and-scripts/spec-lifecycle-automation.md:56:| `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh` | Script | Scores requested work to recommend documentation level and optional phase decomposition |\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/feature-catalog/tooling-and-scripts/phase-system-knowledge-node.md:31:That summary is backed by a deeper reference and executable tooling. `references/structure/phase-definitions.md` expands the taxonomy, folder conventions, phase map/back-reference requirements, and recursive validation expectations. `/speckit:plan :with-phases` (or `/speckit:complete :with-phases`) is the user-facing entry point that drives phase decomposition workflows via optional pre-workflow steps in the plan and complete YAML assets. `create.sh` implements the actual parent-plus-child folder creation path via `--phase`, `--phases`, `--phase-names`, and `--parent`. `recommend-level.sh` calculates both documentation level and the separate default-on phase recommendation fields, while `validate.sh --recursive` checks whether a phased packet is structurally coherent.\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/feature-catalog/tooling-and-scripts/phase-system-knowledge-node.md:48:| `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh` | Script | Computes documentation-level scoring plus the separate phase recommendation and suggested phase count |\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/feature-catalog/feature-catalog.md:626:`create.sh`, `recommend-level.sh`, `check-completion.sh` and `archive.sh` are the entry points.\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/changelog/v2.0.0.0.md:79:- `spec/validate.sh`, `spec/create.sh`, `spec/repair-derived.cjs` and `spec/recommend-level.sh` for the packet lifecycle\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/workflows/quick-reference.md:56:**LOC as one input to `runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh`, which scores it with file count and risk:**\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/workflows/quick-reference.md:576:- **LOC is one scored input** - run `recommend-level.sh` and go higher when your judgment disagrees\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/workflows/intake-contract.md:64:- `level_recommendation` — output of `recommend-level.sh`\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/workflows/intake-contract.md:139:- **Q2. Documentation Level** — recommendation from `recommend-level.sh`; keep or override to Level 1 / 2 / 3 / 3+\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/workflows/intake-contract.md:285:| Recommend-level helper | `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh` |\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/workflows/spec-authoring-card.md:35:bash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh --loc <lines> --files <count>\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/workflows/execution-methods.md:155:### recommend-level.sh\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/workflows/execution-methods.md:162:bash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh \"Add user authentication\"\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/workflows/execution-methods.md:165:bash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh --auth --api \"Add OAuth login\"\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/templates/template-guide.md:104:- <100 LOC, as one input to `recommend-level.sh`\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/templates/template-guide.md:151:- 100-499 LOC, as one input to `recommend-level.sh`\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/templates/template-guide.md:205:- >=500 LOC, as one input to `recommend-level.sh`\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/templates/level-selection-guide.md:38:`runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh` scores tasks across 4 weighted factors (0-100 scale):\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/structure/phase-system.md:32:2. **Documentation level >= 3** (from `recommend-level.sh` 100-point level scoring)\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/structure/phase-system.md:89:| `recommend-level.sh --recommend-phases` | Phase recommendation scoring alongside level       |\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/structure/phase-definitions.md:60:- **Level threshold:** documentation level >= 3 (from `recommend-level.sh` 100-point level scoring)\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/structure/phase-definitions.md:62:> **Scoring systems clarification:** The 50-point phase complexity score (this section) is separate from the 100-point level recommendation score used by `recommend-level.sh`. The level score determines documentation depth (L1/L2/L3/L3+); the phase score determines whether to decompose into child folders. Both thresholds must be met independently.\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh:169:  recommend-level.sh [OPTIONS]\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh:186:  recommend-level.sh --loc 50 --files 2\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh:189:  recommend-level.sh --loc 200 --files 5 --api\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh:192:  recommend-level.sh --loc 500 --files 15 --auth --api --db --architectural\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh:195:  recommend-level.sh --loc 1000 --files 20 --architectural --api --db --recommend-phases\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh:198:  recommend-level.sh --loc 1000 --files 20 --architectural --no-recommend-phases\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh:201:  recommend-level.sh --loc 100 --files 3 --json\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/README.md:67:+-- recommend-level.sh           # Recommend documentation level from task signals\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/manual-testing-playbook/tooling-and-scripts/phase-detection-scoring.md:3:description: \"This scenario validates Phase detection scoring for `PHASE-001`. It focuses on Run `recommend-level.sh --recommend-phases --json` on a high-complexity spec and verify scoring output.\"\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/manual-testing-playbook/tooling-and-scripts/phase-detection-scoring.md:16:This scenario validates Phase detection scoring for `PHASE-001`. It focuses on Run `recommend-level.sh --recommend-phases --json` on a high-complexity spec and verify scoring output.\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/manual-testing-playbook/tooling-and-scripts/phase-detection-scoring.md:23:- Objective: Run `recommend-level.sh --recommend-phases --json` on a high-complexity spec and verify scoring output.\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/manual-testing-playbook/tooling-and-scripts/phase-detection-scoring.md:24:- Real user request: `` Please validate Phase detection scoring against bash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh --recommend-phases --json specs/<target-spec> and tell me whether the expected signals are present: JSON output contains `recommended_phases` (boolean), `phase_score` (number), `suggested_phase_count` (number), and 4 dimension scores: LOC Factor (35%), File Count (20%), Risk Factors (25%), Complexity (20%); simple specs score low. ``\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/manual-testing-playbook/tooling-and-scripts/phase-detection-scoring.md:25:- Prompt: `Validate Phase detection scoring against bash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh --recommend-phases --json specs/<target-spec> and report cited pass/fail evidence.`\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/manual-testing-playbook/tooling-and-scripts/phase-detection-scoring.md:38:Validate Phase detection scoring against bash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh --recommend-phases --json specs/<target-spec> and report cited pass/fail evidence.\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/manual-testing-playbook/tooling-and-scripts/phase-detection-scoring.md:44:2. `bash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh --recommend-phases --json specs/<target-spec>`\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/manual-testing-playbook/tooling-and-scripts/phase-detection-scoring.md:72:Provenance: manual only - bash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh --recommend-phases --json specs/<target-spec>\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/manual-testing-playbook/tooling-and-scripts/spec-lifecycle-automation.md:22:- Real user request: `Please validate Spec Lifecycle Automation against bash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh --help and tell me whether the expected signals are present: help output available for lifecycle entrypoints; upgrade regression suite passes; completeness JSON is emitted; completion gate returns a stable status.`\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/manual-testing-playbook/tooling-and-scripts/spec-lifecycle-automation.md:23:- Prompt: `Validate Spec Lifecycle Automation against bash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh --help and report cited pass/fail evidence.`\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/manual-testing-playbook/tooling-and-scripts/spec-lifecycle-automation.md:36:Valida