{"toolCallId":"call_c45b8086c03041ee9b396f4878bcb201","status":"completed","content":[{"type":"content","content":{"type":"text","text":"./specs/cli-jev/001-cli-jev-creation/goal.md:92:| 2026-09-20 | Packet scaffolded as a Level 3 phase parent with five children, each level set by `recommend-level.sh` |\n./specs/cli-jev/003-cli-jev-workflow-integration/goal.md:208:| 002 level | `recommend-level.sh --loc 200 --files 2` scores Level 0; 002 stays Level 1 because the build-phase criterion requires `plan.md` and `tasks.md`. |\n./specs/cli-jev/003-cli-jev-workflow-integration/001-deep-research/research/research.md:116:| K12 | Row 22, disagreement 7 | \"No decision reads either output\" | The level script reads the flags. The drop stands on low stakes and missing gold | `recommend-level.sh:36-47` |\n./specs/cli-jev/003-cli-jev-workflow-integration/001-deep-research/research/research.md:401:| Spec level | Script policy over caller-supplied flags, which add points to the level | `recommend-level.sh:36-47` | Risk flags | Drop, on low stakes and missing gold |\n./specs/cli-jev/003-cli-jev-workflow-integration/001-deep-research/research/research.md:578:| 7 | A defer shadow log and spec-level flags | MiMo and DeepSeek parked them as later | No decision reads a defer log. The level script does read the flags (`recommend-level.sh:36-47`: auth +10, api +8, db +7, architectural +20), so \"no decision reads either output\" was wrong for the flags | Drop both. The flags drop on low stakes and missing gold for which level a packet should have had, not on a missing reader |\n./specs/cli-jev/003-cli-jev-workflow-integration/001-deep-research/research/research.md:1066:| 22 | Spec-level risk flags beside the level script | The level script reads the flags (auth +10, api +8, db +7, architectural +20), so a Jev flag would change a level. It drops on low stakes and on missing gold for which level a packet should have had, not on a missing reader | Q3, Q11 | `recommend-level.sh:36-47` | DeepSeek parked it as later. Dropped here |\n./specs/cli-jev/003-cli-jev-workflow-integration/001-deep-research/research/research.md:1473:| 180 | `recommend-level.sh:36-47` | Council | resolved | Risk flags add points to the level. Row 22 and disagreement 7 corrected (K12) |\n./specs/cli-jev/003-cli-jev-workflow-integration/001-deep-research/research/research.md:1596:- `runtime/cli/spec-folder/alignment-validator.ts` and `runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh`\n./specs/cli-jev/003-cli-jev-workflow-integration/001-deep-research/research/lineages/mimo/iterations/iteration-006.md:106:| **Value** | Both add a signal to surfaces the operator already resolves fine: `recommend-level.sh` takes four explicit flags whose answers the caller knows, and S25's HIGH issues are already patched by hand. Neither removes a decision; both add a number to check. |\n./specs/cli-jev/003-cli-jev-workflow-integration/001-deep-research/research/lineages/mimo/iterations/iteration-006.md:107:| **Seam** | S24 `recommend-level.sh:19-22` and S25 `save-workflow.md:577-598` (seam-map claims). |\n./specs/cli-jev/003-cli-jev-workflow-integration/001-deep-research/research/lineages/deepseek/findings-registry.json:18:    {\"id\": \"rec-level-flags\", \"title\": \"Spec-level risk flags\", \"verdict\": \"later\", \"seam\": \".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh (digest S24)\", \"harness\": \"gap-gold\", \"loc\": \"40-60\"},\n./specs/cli-jev/003-cli-jev-workflow-integration/001-deep-research/research/lineages/deepseek/research.md:80:9. **Spec-level risk flags — LATER.** `recommend-level.sh` (digest S24); weak gold; policy semantics owned by the script.\n./specs/cli-jev/003-cli-jev-workflow-integration/001-deep-research/research/lineages/deepseek/iterations/iteration-006.md:56:| **Idea** | `noul` per risk flag (\"does this task change authentication / APIs / data / architecture\") so `recommend-level.sh` stops depending on the caller's memory. |\n./specs/cli-jev/003-cli-jev-workflow-integration/001-deep-research/research/lineages/deepseek/iterations/iteration-006.md:57:| **Seam** | S24 `recommend-level.sh:19-22`, `:42-47`, `:106-109` (digest); offline CLI, points map to Levels 0-3. |\n./specs/cli-jev/003-cli-jev-workflow-integration/001-deep-research/ai-council/seats/round-001/seat-001-opus-max.md:123:- **(c) Defer log and spec-level flags.** Both drops hold. The level-flag reason, \"no decision reads either output\" (`research.md:351`), is wrong: each flag adds points that set the level (`recommend-level.sh:19-22`, `:36-47`). The correct reason is low stakes (one documentation tier), no gold and the same task text an agent already reads.\n./specs/cli-jev/003-cli-jev-workflow-integration/001-deep-research/ai-council/seats/round-001/seat-001-opus-max.md:135:| 22 | drop | keep, fix reason | drop | The flags feed the level, so \"no decision reads it\" is wrong. Drop on low stakes and no gold | `recommend-level.sh:19-22`, `:36-47` | Confirmed |\n./specs/cli-jev/003-cli-jev-workflow-integration/001-deep-research/ai-council/seats/round-001/seat-001-opus-max.md:352:  - `recommend-level.sh:15-50`, `:100-112`\n./specs/cli-jev/003-cli-jev-workflow-integration/001-deep-research/ai-council/proposed-resynthesis.md:245:- The level script does read the spec-level flags (`recommend-level.sh:36-47`: auth +10, api +8, db +7, architectural +20), so \"no decision reads either output\" was wrong for the flags.\n./specs/cli-jev/003-cli-jev-workflow-integration/001-deep-research/ai-council/proposed-resynthesis.md:473:  - The level script reads the flags (`recommend-level.sh:36-47`: auth +10, api +8, db +7, architectural +20), so a Jev flag would change a level.\n./specs/cli-jev/003-cli-jev-workflow-integration/001-deep-research/ai-council/proposed-resynthesis.md:475:  - The evidence becomes `recommend-level.sh:36-47`.\n./specs/cli-jev/003-cli-jev-workflow-integration/001-deep-research/ai-council/proposed-resynthesis.md:637:| 157 | `recommend-level.sh:36-47` | Council | resolved | Flags feed the level. Row 22 and disagreement 7 corrected |\n./specs/cli-jev/003-cli-jev-workflow-integration/001-deep-research/ai-council/council-report.md:133:| 22 spec-level flags | keep, correct the reason | The flags do feed the level (auth +10, api +8, db +7, architectural +20). The drop stands on low stakes and no gold | `recommend-level.sh:36-47` H | Confirmed |\n./specs/cli-jev/003-cli-jev-workflow-integration/001-deep-research/ai-council/deliberations/round-001.md:83:| Level flags feed the level | 001 | `recommend-level.sh:36-47` (auth +10, api +8, db +7, architectural +20) | Confirmed. research.md's reason \"no decision reads\" is wrong |\n./specs/cli-jev/003-cli-jev-workflow-integration/005-compaction-recall-harness/goal.md:142:| Level 1 has no `acceptance-criteria.md` | The criteria above come from `spec.md` REQ-001 to REQ-007, its stop line and its proof plan. `recommend-level.sh --loc 730 --files 9` scores Level 1 |\n./specs/agents/010-repo-rule-system-integration/research/lineages/deepseek/prior-findings.md:26:- AGENTS.md's external targets resolve: `gate-3-classifier.ts`, `lookup-trigger-index.mjs`, `skill-advisor-hook.md`, `code-quality-standards.md`, `skill-root-metadata-contract.md`, `parent-skills-nested-packets.md`, `retrieval-conventions.md`, `validate.sh`, `recommend-level.sh`, `folder-structure.md`, `folder-routing.md`, `phase-definitions.md`, `agent-io-contract.md`, `save-workflow.md`, `generate-context.js`, `sk-code/SKILL.md` §2 SMART ROUTING (:50), and system-spec-kit/SKILL.md's \"Distributed Governance Rule\" (:59).\n./specs/agents/010-repo-rule-system-integration/research/lineages/deepseek/iterations/iteration-002.md:28:3. **A repo verification-commands rule** — refused **test 4**: no named failure. `AGENTS.md:182` describes the class (\"verification commands and local contracts\"), and the commands already exist and are cited (`AGENTS.md:266` `validate.sh`; `:375` `recommend-level.sh`; `:472` `generate-trigger-index.mjs`), all verified present this run.\n./specs/agents/010-repo-rule-system-integration/research/lineages/deepseek/iterations/iteration-001.md:86:- AGENTS.md's external targets resolve: `gate-3-classifier.ts`, `lookup-trigger-index.mjs`, `skill-advisor-hook.md`, `code-quality-standards.md`, `skill-root-metadata-contract.md`, `parent-skills-nested-packets.md`, `retrieval-conventions.md`, `validate.sh`, `recommend-level.sh`, `folder-structure.md`, `folder-routing.md`, `phase-definitions.md`, `agent-io-contract.md`, `save-workflow.md`, `generate-context.js`, `sk-code/SKILL.md` §2 SMART ROUTING (:50), and system-spec-kit/SKILL.md's \"Distributed Governance Rule\" (:59).\n./specs/agents/008-orchestrate-external-cli-delegation/implementation-summary.md:117:| Went to Level 2 against a Level 0 score | `recommend-level.sh` scored 24/100. The verification burden, not the edit size, is what this packet actually is, and sibling 007 sets Level 2 for the same file. |\n\u001b[0m[... 462 lines (8060 KB) omitted ...]\n./specs/cli-external-orchestration/z_archive/061-glm-5-3-flash-thinking-tier-per-route/spec.md:48:> **Level basis.** `recommend-level.sh --loc 40 --files 5 --api` scored 21/100, Level 0. Taken to Level 1 deliberately: the change alters live dispatch behavior on a runtime contract shared by every pi fan-out lineage, and the scoring inputs do not see that. Where the script and judgment differ, the rule is to go higher.\n./specs/cli-external-orchestration/z_archive/066-pi-self-dispatch-and-subagents-retirement/plan.md:238:Total ≈ 30 files, ≈ 320 lines. Level 2 by `recommend-level.sh --loc 320 --files 30 --api`:\n./specs/cli-external-orchestration/z_archive/060-devpass-roster-vision-gemini-3-8/spec.md:55:> **Level basis.** `recommend-level.sh --loc 300 --files 18 --api` returned **Level 2 (Verification)**, score 48/100, confidence 82%, phase score 10/50 (threshold 25) — phases NOT recommended. Re-scored at `--loc 420 --files 26 --api` after the 2026-09-04 scope amendment: still **Level 2**, and the phase score stays below threshold. This is a standard packet, not a phase parent.\n./specs/sk-git/033-git-setup-customization/005-setup-check-hardening/spec.md:235:| **Total** | **33/70** | **Level 2**, from `recommend-level.sh --loc 480 --files 15 --api`, score 52 |\n./.skilled/changelog/skilled/v4.0.0.0.md:82:- `spec/validate.sh`, `spec/create.sh`, `spec/repair-derived.cjs` and `spec/recommend-level.sh` for the packet lifecycle\n./.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/feature-catalog/tooling-and-scripts/spec-lifecycle-automation.md:6:  - recommend-level.sh\n./.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/feature-catalog/tooling-and-scripts/spec-lifecycle-automation.md:19:The lifecycle is intentionally split into focused commands. `recommend-level.sh` scores a task and recommends the documentation level and optional phasing strategy. `create.sh` materializes the parent spec, optional child phases, or versioned subfolders. `upgrade-level.sh` raises an existing spec folder to a richer documentation level without discarding authored content. `calculate-completeness.sh` measures placeholder burn-down and optional content quality, `check-completion.sh` enforces checklist completion and evidence rules, and `archive.sh` archives or restores completed work with a completeness gate.\n./.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/feature-catalog/tooling-and-scripts/spec-lifecycle-automation.md:29:Level recommendation is handled by `recommend-level.sh` as a standalone scoring tool. It accepts estimated LOC, file count, and risk flags for auth, API, database, and architectural work, converts those inputs into a 100-point score, maps the result to Level 0 through Level 3, and separately computes whether phased execution is recommended. Phase scoring uses its own 50-point signal model and only recommends phases when the phase score crosses the threshold and the recommended documentation level is Level 3 or higher.\n./.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/feature-catalog/tooling-and-scripts/spec-lifecycle-automation.md:31:Spec creation is handled by `create.sh`, which defaults to Level 1 unless `--level` is provided. The script creates `scratch/`, copies the level template set, optionally creates a git branch and writes `description.json` when the Node helper is available. For root and phase scaffolds it then derives `graph-metadata.json` through the graph backfill, which warns and continues when the derivation fails. It also replaces the template placeholder trigger phrases of 18 document kinds with phrases built from the packet slug, and it runs full post-create validation only when `SPECKIT_POST_VALIDATE=1` is set. Beyond normal folder creation, it supports versioned subfolders with `--subfolder`, phased parent-plus-child creation with `--phase`, append-mode phase growth with `--parent`, named child phases with `--phase-names`, and Level 3 sharded spec sections with `--sharded`. The current implementation exposes complexity fields in its output, but the script itself still depends on explicit `--level` input rather than invoking `recommend-level.sh` automatically.\n./.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/feature-catalog/tooling-and-scripts/spec-lifecycle-automation.md:56:| `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh` | Script | Scores requested work to recommend documentation level and optional phase decomposition |\n./.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/feature-catalog/tooling-and-scripts/phase-system-knowledge-node.md:31:That summary is backed by a deeper reference and executable tooling. `references/structure/phase-definitions.md` expands the taxonomy, folder conventions, phase map/back-reference requirements, and recursive validation expectations. `/speckit:plan :with-phases` (or `/speckit:complete :with-phases`) is the user-facing entry point that drives phase decomposition workflows via optional pre-workflow steps in the plan and complete YAML assets. `create.sh` implements the actual parent-plus-child folder creation path via `--phase`, `--phases`, `--phase-names`, and `--parent`. `recommend-level.sh` calculates both documentation level and the separate default-on phase recommendation fields, while `validate.sh --recursive` checks whether a phased packet is structurally coherent.\n./.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/feature-catalog/tooling-and-scripts/phase-system-knowledge-node.md:48:| `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh` | Script | Computes documentation-level scoring plus the separate phase recommendation and suggested phase count |\n./.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/feature-catalog/feature-catalog.md:626:`create.sh`, `recommend-level.sh`, `check-completion.sh` and `archive.sh` are the entry points.\n./.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/changelog/v2.0.0.0.md:79:- `spec/validate.sh`, `spec/create.sh`, `spec/repair-derived.cjs` and `spec/recommend-level.sh` for the packet lifecycle\n./.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/workflows/quick-reference.md:56:**LOC as one input to `runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh`, which scores it with file count and risk:**\n./.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/workflows/quick-reference.md:576:- **LOC is one scored input** - run `recommend-level.sh` and go higher when your judgment disagrees\n./.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/workflows/intake-contract.md:64:- `level_recommendation` — output of `recommend-level.sh`\n./.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/workflows/intake-contract.md:139:- **Q2. Documentation Level** — recommendation from `recommend-level.sh`; keep or override to Level 1 / 2 / 3 / 3+\n./.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/workflows/intake-contract.md:285:| Recommend-level helper | `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh` |\n./.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/workflows/spec-authoring-card.md:35:bash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh --loc <lines> --files <count>\n./.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/workflows/execution-methods.md:155:### recommend-level.sh\n./.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/workflows/execution-methods.md:162:bash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh \"Add user authentication\"\n./.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/workflows/execution-methods.md:165:bash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh --auth --api \"Add OAuth login\"\n./.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/templates/template-guide.md:104:- <100 LOC, as one input to `recommend-level.sh`\n./.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/templates/template-guide.md:151:- 100-499 LOC, as one input to `recommend-level.sh`\n./.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/templates/template-guide.md:205:- >=500 LOC, as one input to `recommend-level.sh`\n./.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/templates/level-selection-guide.md:38:`runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh` scores tasks across 4 weighted factors (0-100 scale):\n./.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/structure/phase-system.md:32:2. **Documentation level >= 3** (from `recommend-level.sh` 100-point level scoring)\n./.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/structure/phase-system.md:89:| `recommend-level.sh --recommend-phases` | Phase recommendation scoring alongside level       |\n./.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/structure/phase-definitions.md:60:- **Level threshold:** documentation level >= 3 (from `recommend-level.sh` 100-point level scoring)\n./.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/structure/phase-definitions.md:62:> **Scoring systems clarification:** The 50-point phase complexity score (this section) is separate from the 100-point level recommendation score used by `recommend-level.sh`. The level score determines documentation depth (L1/L2/L3/L3+); the phase score determines whether to decompose into child folders. Both thresholds must be met independently.\n./.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh:169:  recommend-level.sh [OPTIONS]\n./.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh:186:  recommend-level.sh --loc 50 --files 2\n./.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh:189:  recommend-level.sh --loc 200 --files 5 --api\n./.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh:192:  recommend-level.sh --loc 500 --files 15 --auth --api --db --architectural\n./.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh:195:  recommend-level.sh --loc 1000 --files 20 --architectural --api --db --recommend-phases\n./.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh:198:  recommend-level.sh --loc 1000 --files 20 --architectural --no-recommend-phases\n./.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh:201:  recommend-level.sh --loc 100 --files 3 --json\n./.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/README.md:67:+-- recommend-level.sh           # Recommend documentation level from task signals\n./.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/retrieval/fixtures/phrase-variants.json:79714:      \"recommend-level.sh\"\n./.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/manual-testing-playbook/tooling-and-scripts/phase-detection-scoring.md:3:description: \"This scenario validates Phase detection scoring for `PHASE-001`. It focuses on Run `recommend-level.sh --recommend-phases --json` on a high-complexity spec and verify scoring output.\"\n./.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/manual-testing-playbook/tooling-and-scripts/phase-detection-scoring.md:16:This scenario validates Phase detection scoring for `PHASE-001`. It focuses on Run `recommend-level.sh --recommend-phases --json` on a high-complexity spec and verify scoring output.\n./.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/manual-testing-playbook/tooling-and-scripts/phase-detection-scoring.md:23:- Objective: Run `recommend-level.sh --recommend-phases --json` on a high-complexity spec and verify scoring output.\n./.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/manual-testing-playbook/tooling-and-scripts/phase-detection-scoring.md:24:- Real user request: `` Please validate Phase detection scoring against bash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh --recommend-phases --json specs/<target-spec> and tell me whether the expected signals are present: JSON output contains `recommended_phases` (boolean), `phase_score` (number), `suggested_phase_count` (number), and 4 dimension scores: LOC Factor (35%), File Count (20%), Risk Factors (25%), Complexity (20%); simple specs score low. ``\n./.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/manual-testing-playbook/tooling-and-scripts/phase-detection-scoring.md:25:- Prompt: `Validate Phase detection scoring against bash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh --recommend-phases --json specs/<target-spec> and report cited pass/fail evidence.`\n./.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/manual-testing-playbook/tooling-and-scripts/phase-detection-scoring.md:38:Validate Phase detection scoring against bash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh --recommend-phases --json specs/<target-spec> and report cited pass/fail evidence.\n./.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/manual-testing-playbook/tooling-and-scripts/phase-detection-scoring.md:44:2. `bash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh --recommend-phases --json specs/<target-spec>`\n./.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/manual-testing-playbook/tooling-and-scripts/phase-detection-scoring.md:72:Provenance: manual only - bash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh --recommend-phases --json specs/<target-spec>\n./.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/manual-testing-playbook/tooling-and-scripts/spec-lifecycle-automation.md:22:- Real user request: `Please validate Spec Lifecycle Automation against bash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh --help and tell me whether the expected signals are present: help output available for lifecycle entrypoints; upgrade regression suite passes; completeness JSON is emitted; completion gate returns a stable status.`\n./.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/manual-testing-playbook/tooling-and-scripts/spec-lifecycle-automation.md:23:- Prompt: `Validate Spec Lifecycle Automation against bash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh --help and report cited pass/fail evidence.`\n./.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/manual-testing-playbook/tooling-and-scripts/spec-lifecycle-automation.md:36:Validate Spec Lifecycle Automation against bash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh --help and report cited pass/fail evidence.\n./.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/manual-testing-playbook/tooling-and-scripts/spec-lifecycle-automation.md:41:1. `bash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh --help`\n./.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/manual-testing-playbook/tooling-and-scripts/spec-lifecycle-automation.md:53:Command 1: `bash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh --help`\n./.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/manual-testing-playbook/tooling-and-scripts/spec-lifecycle-automation.md:61:  recommend-level.sh [OPTIONS]\n./.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/manual-testing-playbook/tooling-and-scripts/spec-lifecycle-automation.md:78:  recommend-level.sh --loc 50 --files 2\n./.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/manual-testing-playbook/tooling-and-scripts/spec-lifecycle-automation.md:81:  recommend-level.sh --loc 200 --files 5 --api\n./.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/manual-testing-playbook/tooling-and-scripts/spec-lifecycle-automation.md:84:  recommend-level.sh --loc 500 --files 15 --auth --api --db --architectural\n./.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/manual-testing-playbook/tooling-and-scripts/spec-lifecycle-automation.md:87:  recommend-level.sh --loc 1000 --files 20 --architectural --api --db --recommend-phases\n./.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/manual-testing-playbook/tooling-and-scripts/spec-lifecycle-automation.md:90:  recommend-level.sh --loc 1000 --files 20 --architectural --no-recommend-phases\n./.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/manual-testing-playbook/tooling-and-scripts/spec-lifecycle-automation.md:93:  recommend-level.sh --loc 100 --files 3 --json\n./.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/manual-testing-playbook/tooling-and-scripts/spec-lifecycle-automation.md:232:Inspect `runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh`, `runtime/cli/tests/test-upgrade-level.sh`, `runtime/cli/spec/calculate-completeness.sh`, and `runtime/cli/spec/archive.sh` if a lifecycle stage is missing or inconsistent\n./.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/manual-testing-playbook/tooling-and-scripts/spec-lifecycle-automation.md:240:Provenance: manual only - bash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh --help\n./.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/manual-testing-playbook/tooling-and-scripts/phase-command-workflow.md:44:2. Verify Step 1: Phase scoring runs (recommend-level.sh --recommend-phases)\n./.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/manual-testing-playbook/tooling-and-scripts/phase-command-workflow.md:61:$ bash \".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh\" --json --recommend-phases --phase-threshold 0.6 --loc 500 --files 8\n./.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/manual-testing-playbook/tooling-and-scripts/phase-command-workflow.md:66:$ bash \".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh\" --json --recommend-phases --phase-threshold 300 --loc 500 --files 8\n./.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/manual-testing-playbook/template-authoring/level-1-packet-authored-from-card.md:74:BANNED OPERATIONS: git commit, git push, git checkout, git switch, git branch, git reset, git stash, generate-context.js, /speckit:save, and any edit outside specs/zz-pb-card/. Do not edit recommend-level.sh. Do not edit anything under .skilled/.\n./.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/manual-testing-playbook/template-authoring/level-1-packet-authored-from-card.md:79:3. Fill spec.md, plan.md, tasks.md and implementation-summary.md. Describe this feature in the packet and do not build it: a --quiet flag for .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh that prints only the final recommended-level line. Say in implementation-summary.md that the packet is planned and not implemented.\n./.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/README.md:514:bash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh specs/[project]/NNN-feature/\n./.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/README.md:621:| `recommend-level.sh` | analyze scope and risk to recommend the right level |\n./.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/SKILL.md:114:- `spec/recommend-level.sh`\n./.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/assets/level-decision-matrix.md:302:**LOC as one input to `recommend-level.sh`, which scores LOC, file count and risk together:**\n./.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/assets/template-mapping.md:297:Run `runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh`, which scores LOC, file count and risk; go higher when it disagrees with your judgment\n./.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-skilled/references/shared/code-organization/directory-and-test-conventions.md:203:│   ├── recommend-level.sh\n./README.md:423:- **`recommend-level.sh`** - analyze scope and risk to recommend the right documentation level\n./AGENTS.md:251:| **Which level does this work need?**                                | `system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh` — deterministic scoring over LOC, file count and risk. |\n./.hermes/skills/system-spec-kit/SKILL.md:119:- `spec/recommend-level.sh`\n"}}],"_meta":{"cognition.ai/cwd":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w1eb206b128/tree","terminal_exit":{"terminal_id":"8073d7","exit_code":0,"signal":null},"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"exec"}}
