{"toolCallId":"call_d71d6e38b51a448fa16e6e1f09c117f8","status":"completed","content":[{"type":"content","content":{"type":"text","text":"{\n  \"args\": [\"--loc\", \"700\", \"--files\", \"16\", \"--architectural\", \"--api\", \"--db\", \"--recommend-phases\", \"--json\"],\n  \"expected\": {\n    \"recommended_phases\": true,\n    \"phase_score\": 30,\n    \"suggested_phase_count\": 2\n  }\n}\n"}}],"_meta":{"cognition.ai/cwd":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w1eb206b128/tree","terminal_exit":{"terminal_id":"87eecb","exit_code":0,"signal":null},"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"exec"}}
{"toolCallId":"call_d72add2ce54348bcbe9fe3db6e990ed2","status":"completed","content":[{"type":"content","content":{"type":"text","text":"- `implementation-summary.md` states what changed and how it was checked. Write it last.\n\nDo not put a task list in `spec.md`. Do not put requirements in `plan.md`.\n\nAcceptance: every heading in the packet has content under it, and no heading holds content that belongs to another heading.\nVerify: `rg -n '^## ' <packet folder>/spec.md <packet folder>/plan.md` lists the headings you filled.\n\n## 6. THE PLAN SHAPE\n\nA plan has 3 or 4 steps. More than 4 steps means the feature is too large for one packet. Split it or raise the level.\n\nEach step carries three lines:\n1. What the step does.\n2. The acceptance line: what is true when the step is done.\n3. The verify command: the command a reader runs, and the text it prints.\n\n```markdown\n### Step 1: Add the flag parser\n\nAcceptance: `--quiet` is accepted and the default output is unchanged.\nVerify: `bash script.sh --quiet` prints one line.\n```\n\nAcceptance: `plan.md` holds 3 or 4 steps, and each step has an acceptance line and a verify command.\nVerify: `rg -c '^### Step ' <packet folder>/plan.md` prints 3 or 4.\n\n## 7. TASK LINES\n\nEvery task line has one action, one file and one verify clause.\n\n```markdown\n- [ ] T001 Add the quiet flag to the option parser (`runtime/cli/spec/script.sh`). Verify: `bash runtime/cli/spec/script.sh --quiet` prints one line.\n```\n\nRules:\n- One action per task.\n- Name the file in parentheses.\n- End with `Verify:` and the command plus its expected output.\n- Put the tasks in the order you will run them.\n- Mark a task `[x]` only after its verify command printed the expected output.\n\nAcceptance: every task line ends with a `Verify:` clause.\nVerify: `rg -c 'Verify: ' <packet folder>/tasks.md` and `rg -c '^- \\[ \\] T[0-9]' <packet folder>/tasks.md` print the same number.\n\n## 8. FILL EVERY TOKEN\n\nA scaffold stamped `v2.3` or later carries tokens. A token starts with `[YOUR_VALUE_HERE:` and ends at the next closing bracket. Replace the whole token, brackets included, with real content. Do not leave a token in a finished packet.\n\nIf you cannot answer a question the token asks, write `UNKNOWN` in its place and write an open question in `goal.md` section 4.\n\nA token in a packet whose `spec.md` says `Status: Draft` is a warning, so strict validation can pass with tokens still in the file. A token in any other status is an error. Do not use the warning as permission. Count the tokens.\n\nAcceptance: the count is 0.\nVerify: `rg -o '\\[YOUR_VALUE_HERE: ' <packet folder>/spec.md <packet folder>/plan.md <packet folder>/tasks.md | wc -l` prints 0.\n\n## 9. VALIDATE\n\nRun the validator before you claim the packet is done.\n\n```bash\nbash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/validate.sh <packet folder> --strict\n```\n\nThe last line must be `RESULT: PASSED`. Read the summary line above it. `Errors: 0` is the pass condition. Warnings do not block the pass, but read them.\n\nWhen it fails, read the first failing rule. Fix that rule only. Run the command again. Stop after three fixes on the same rule and write the rule and the error in the packet's `goal.md`.\n\nAcceptance: the command prints `RESULT: PASSED` and `Errors: 0`.\nVerify: `bash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/validate.sh <packet folder> --strict | tail -1` prints `RESULT: PASSED`.\n\n## 10. CLOSE\n\nA packet is closeable when:\n- every required file exists for its level\n- every token is filled, or replaced with `UNKNOWN` and an open question in `goal.md`\n- `tasks.md` has no `[B]` line\n- `implementation-summary.md` names the files that changed\n- `validate.sh --strict` prints `RESULT: PASSED`\n\nAcceptance: all five are true.\nVerify: run the five commands in this card in order, then run the validator once more. The last line prints `RESULT: PASSED`.\n\n## 11. WHEN TO STOP AND ASK\n\nStop and write the question in `goal.md` when:\n- two documents in the packet state opposite rules\n- a command in the plan would write outside the packet folder\n- the validator fails on the same rule after three fixes\n- the feature needs more than 4 plan steps\n\nAcceptance: the question is written in `goal.md` as `Open question:` under the rule or command that raised it.\nVerify: `rg -n 'Open question:' <packet folder>/goal.md` prints at least one line.\nDo not guess. A written question is a finished step. A guess is a defect.\n"}}],"_meta":{"cognition.ai/cwd":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w1eb206b128/tree","terminal_exit":{"terminal_id":"29f9b5","exit_code":0,"signal":null},"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"exec"}}
{"toolCallId":"call_d86d80df497a4636834b77360d294028","status":"completed","content":[{"type":"content","content":{"type":"text","text":".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/workflows/spec-authoring-card.md:124:## 8. FILL EVERY TOKEN\n"}}],"_meta":{"cognition.ai/cwd":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w1eb206b128/tree","terminal_exit":{"terminal_id":"c8ec56","exit_code":0,"signal":null},"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"exec"}}
{"toolCallId":"call_d8a1d0711de9415bbdc0839ce8ae528b","status":"completed","content":[{"type":"content","content":{"type":"text","text":"---\ntitle: \"Feature Specification: Add User Authentication\"\ndescription: \"Level 3 spec example adding an executive summary, risk matrix and user stories.\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"feature specification\"\n  - \"problem statement\"\n  - \"requirements and scope\"\n  - \"user authentication\"\nimportance_tier: \"normal\"\ncontextType: \"general\"\n---\n# Feature Specification: Add User Authentication\n\n<!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 3 -->\n<!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: spec-core + level2-verify + level3-arch | v2.2 -->\n\n<!-- EXAMPLE: This is a filled-in Level 3 spec demonstrating architecture-focused\ndocumentation. Note the addition of Executive Summary, Risk Matrix, User Stories,\nand cross-references to decision records. Use this for complex features (500+ LOC). -->\n\n---\n\n## EXECUTIVE SUMMARY\n\nThis specification covers the implementation of a comprehensive user authentication system for the application. The system will support email/password registration and login, secure password storage with bcrypt, and JWT-based session management. This is a foundational feature that enables all future user-specific functionality including personalization, user preferences, and access control.\n\n**Key Decisions**: JWT over sessions for stateless auth (ADR-001), bcrypt with 10 rounds for password hashing (ADR-002)\n\n**Critical Dependencies**: PostgreSQL database, bcrypt library\n\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:metadata -->\n## 1. METADATA\n\n| Field | Value |\n|-------|-------|\n| **Level** | 3 |\n| **Priority** | P0 |\n| **Status** | Complete |\n| **Created** | 2025-01-15 |\n| **Branch** | `012-user-authentication` |\n| **Estimated LOC** | ~600 |\n\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:metadata -->\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:problem -->\n## 2. PROBLEM & PURPOSE\n\n### Problem Statement\nThe application currently has no user authentication, allowing anyone to access all features without identity verification. This creates security vulnerabilities, prevents personalization features from being implemented, and blocks the development of user-specific functionality such as saved preferences, order history, and account management.\n\n### Purpose\nImplement a production-ready email/password authentication system that provides secure user registration, login, and session management while establishing patterns and infrastructure for future authentication enhancements.\n\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:problem -->\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:scope -->\n## 3. SCOPE\n\n### In Scope\n- User registration with email and password\n- User login with session management\n- Password hashing using bcrypt\n- JWT token generation and validation\n- Input validation with clear error messages\n- Protection against common attacks (SQL injection, timing attacks)\n- Database schema for user storage\n- Auth middleware for protected routes\n\n### Out of Scope\n- Social login (OAuth) - spec/013-oauth-integration\n- Password reset functionality - spec/014-password-reset\n- Two-factor authentication - future enhancement\n- Role-based permissions - spec/015-rbac\n- Email verification - requires email service\n\n### Files to Change\n\n| File Path | Change Type | Description |\n|-----------|-------------|-------------|\n| src/auth/register.js | Create | Registration form and API handler |\n| src/auth/login.js | Create | Login form and session creation |\n| src/auth/logout.js | Create | Session termination |\n| src/utils/hash.js | Create | Password hashing utilities |\n| src/utils/token.js | Create | JWT generation and validation |\n| src/middleware/auth.js | Create | Authentication middleware |\n| src/validators/auth.js | Create | Input validation schemas |\n| prisma/schema.prisma | Modify | Add User model |\n| tests/ | Create | Unit and integration tests |\n\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:scope -->\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:requirements -->\n## 4. REQUIREMENTS\n\n### P0 - Blockers (MUST complete)\n\n| ID | Requirement |\n|----|-------------|\n| REQ-001 | Users can register with email/password |\n| REQ-002 | Users can log in with valid credentials |\n| REQ-003 | Passwords are hashed before storage |\n| REQ-004 | Input validation prevents malformed data |\n| REQ-005 | Protected routes require authentication |\n\n### P1 - Required (complete OR user-approved deferral)\n\n| ID | Requirement |\n|----|-------------|\n| REQ-006 | Invalid login shows appropriate error |\n| REQ-007 | Session persists across page refresh |\n| REQ-008 | Duplicate email registration prevented |\n"}}],"_meta":{"cognition.ai/cwd":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w1eb206b128/tree","terminal_exit":{"terminal_id":"419c94","exit_code":0,"signal":null},"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"exec"}}
